  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "Using a D-Wave Leap hybrid CQM solver on a 60-asset cross-market portfolio, the quantum annealing-based method achieves an average normalized hypervolume of 0.697, hypervolume rate of 98.02%, IGD of 0.00476, and about 92 non-dominated solutions in 0.337 seconds per run, while the broader cross-market setting reaches an average HV of 0.725 and HV rate of 98.34%. On specific months, the cross-market configuration attains HV up to 0.877 with HV rate 99.95% and IGD as low as 0.0012, indicating high-quality Pareto fronts that are competitive with classical MOEAs but do not clearly demonstrate a sustained quantum advantage.",
